Purchases's live database name and username come from Console's SaaS Database Details, not from DB_NAME
and DB_USER in .env, so the SDK's .env-driven CLI (analytics-platform-collect.php) would report the
size of whichever database .env happens to name — usually a developer's local one, or nothing at
all, because .env here carries no DB_NAME to find.

tests/console_database.php also asserts that exactly ONE file in src/ and bin/ builds a database
connection (src/Db.php), so merely shipping that CLI fails the suite.

bin/analytics-platform-snapshot.php reports this product's database figures instead, through
Db::connect() — the same connection the API itself uses, on the database Console named.
install-analytics-sdk.sh reads this marker on every run, so a refresh never puts the CLI back.
